{
  "format": "lavernus-leabhar",
  "version": 3,
  "title": "The Last Stable State",
  "startNodeId": 1,
  "variables": {
    "HasPebble": "none",
    "ToldMira": "none",
    "BridgeAnswer": "none",
    "ThroughputAnswer": "none",
    "PressureAnswer": "none",
    "CourtyardOutcome": "none",
    "PowerReleased": "none"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "The Banana Incident",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Lavernus Academy, in the scholarly region of Lurralde. Practical Magic II is supposed to be a quiet morning.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Today's exercise is containment geometry under live mana flux. Nobody improvises. Nobody increases input without permission.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "Tavian, your left stabilizer is crooked.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "I know. I'm fixing it.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian takes one step backward.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "Why is there a banana peel in a ritual classroom?",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "His heel shoots forward. He falls backward hard enough that the room vanishes into a white flash.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The back of his head strikes a small pebble lodged between two floor tiles. Warm blood runs into his collar before anyone reaches him.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Do not move him. Cut the practice lattice. Mira, infirmary bell. Now.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Under Tavian's blood, a hair-thin spiral hidden inside the pebble shines once, then goes dark.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": null,
      "defaultChildId": 2,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "name": "One Week Later",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "A week later, Tavian is discharged from the academy hospital with twelve stitches, a headache, and strict instructions not to fall over again.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "I brought your notes. Also, the class has collectively agreed the banana was attempted murder by breakfast.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "Good. I was worried I lost a duel to fruit.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "As Tavian reaches for his coat, the ward-light above his bed flickers. He touches the metal bedrail.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The flicker stops. Not because the lamp repairs itself. The failing mana pattern simply... stays exactly as it is.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "Mira.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "Yes?",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "Nothing.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 1,
      "defaultChildId": 3,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "name": "Back at Lavernus Academy",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The academy looks offensively normal. Students hurry between towers. Ritual motors hum under the pavement. Someone has already replaced the cracked classroom tile.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "Ritual Science Theory starts in fifteen minutes. If Vask sees you late after being medically excused for a week, she will still mark you late.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "That sounds like her.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 2,
      "defaultChildId": 5,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_go_class",
          "text": "Go straight to Ritual Science Theory.",
          "targetId": 5,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_old_room",
          "text": "Visit the old practicum room first.",
          "targetId": 4,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "name": "Old Practicum Room",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The practicum room is empty. The banana peel is gone. The stain is not.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Near the repaired tile, the pebble still sits in a shallow crack. It is smaller than Tavian remembers.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "I nearly died because of you.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Under the light, one side of the pebble carries grooves too regular to be natural: a tiny spiral interrupted by one deliberate gap.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 3,
      "defaultChildId": 5,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_leave_pebble",
          "text": "Leave it alone.",
          "targetId": 5,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_take_pebble",
          "text": "Pocket the pebble.",
          "targetId": 5,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "HasPebble",
              "value": "true"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_trace_grooves",
          "text": "Trace the chipped grooves with your finger.",
          "targetId": 30,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "name": "Ritual Science Theory",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Ritual science is not the art of making circles look impressive. It is the study of measurable mana behavior.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Today: conversion loss, throughput, and field pressure. These are three different ways to destroy expensive equipment.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "First problem. A mana-energy bridge loses ninety-nine percent of incoming converted mana. Your load requires twenty Ma on the far side.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "How much mana must enter the bridge?",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 3,
      "defaultChildId": 6,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "name": "Quiz: Bridge Loss",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "No guessing. If ninety-nine percent is lost, one percent survives. The load still needs twenty Ma.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 5,
      "defaultChildId": null,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_bridge_2000",
          "text": "2,000 Ma.",
          "targetId": 7,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "BridgeAnswer",
              "value": "correct"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_bridge_200",
          "text": "200 Ma.",
          "targetId": 8,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "BridgeAnswer",
              "value": "wrong"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_bridge_20",
          "text": "20 Ma.",
          "targetId": 8,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "BridgeAnswer",
              "value": "wrong"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "name": "Bridge Answer: Correct",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Correct. Twenty is one percent of two thousand. Twenty divided by 0.01 gives two thousand Ma input.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "I hate bridges.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Good. Respect is the beginning of engineering.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 6,
      "defaultChildId": 9,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "name": "Bridge Answer: Correction",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "No. The bridge delivers only one percent of what enters it. Twenty divided by 0.01 is two thousand Ma.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "A two-order-of-magnitude mistake is not a small rounding error. It is a crater.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 6,
      "defaultChildId": 9,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "name": "Quiz: Capacity vs Throughput",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Second problem. An accumulator can store one hundred Ma. Its regulating lacery accepts at most ten Ma per second.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "You feed it twenty Ma per second for three seconds. Assume no output during those three seconds. What fails first?",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 7,
      "defaultChildId": null,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_throughput_correct",
          "text": "The regulator can fail. Only 60 Ma is stored, but 20 Ma/s exceeds the safe input throughput.",
          "targetId": 10,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "ThroughputAnswer",
              "value": "correct"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_throughput_safe",
          "text": "Nothing. Sixty Ma is below the 100 Ma capacity.",
          "targetId": 11,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "ThroughputAnswer",
              "value": "wrong"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_throughput_overflow",
          "text": "The accumulator overflows because 20 × 3 is more than 100.",
          "targetId": 11,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "ThroughputAnswer",
              "value": "wrong"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "name": "Throughput Answer: Correct",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Exactly. Capacity and throughput are different limits. Sixty Ma fits. Twenty Ma per second does not.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "You can overwhelm regulating lacery without filling the accumulator.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 9,
      "defaultChildId": 12,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "name": "Throughput Answer: Correction",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "The stored amount is only sixty Ma, so capacity is not the problem.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "The input is twice the safe throughput. The regulator may fail while the accumulator itself remains far from full.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 9,
      "defaultChildId": 12,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "name": "Quiz: Field Pressure",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Last one. In this apparatus, mana-field pressure is proportional to the square of field intensity.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "If field intensity doubles, what happens to pressure?",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 10,
      "defaultChildId": null,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_pressure_4",
          "text": "Pressure becomes four times greater.",
          "targetId": 13,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "PressureAnswer",
              "value": "correct"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_pressure_2",
          "text": "Pressure doubles.",
          "targetId": 14,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "PressureAnswer",
              "value": "wrong"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_pressure_8",
          "text": "Pressure becomes eight times greater.",
          "targetId": 14,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "PressureAnswer",
              "value": "wrong"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "name": "Pressure Answer: Correct",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Correct. Double M means four times M squared. This is why 'just add more mana' is not a design philosophy.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 12,
      "defaultChildId": 15,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "name": "Pressure Answer: Correction",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "No. Pressure follows M squared. Doubling M gives two squared, so pressure becomes four times greater.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Remember that before you volunteer to tune a compression stage.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 12,
      "defaultChildId": 15,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "name": "The Hallway Ward",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "After class, a corridor ward begins stuttering between active and inactive states.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "Maintenance has ignored that thing for three weeks.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian presses two fingers to the ward plate.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Something inside him catches the mana pattern and holds it. The flicker freezes. For six impossible seconds, the damaged ward cannot drift from the exact configuration it had when he touched it.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "I can make magic stay put.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "That is not a sentence people are normally allowed to say.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 13,
      "defaultChildId": 16,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_tell_mira",
          "text": "Tell Mira about the hospital lamp too.",
          "targetId": 16,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "ToldMira",
              "value": "true"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_hide_detail",
          "text": "Say this is the first time it happened.",
          "targetId": 16,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "name": "Fixation",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Pattern fixation.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Vask has Tavian repeat the trick on a harmless training lattice. The lattice refuses to decay until Tavian lets go.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Useful. Dangerous. You are not creating mana. You are forcing an existing configuration to remain its own reference.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "Can people normally do that?",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "No.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Do not test it on living tissue, high-compression arrays, or anything connected to a city-scale calibration network.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 15,
      "defaultChildId": 17,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "name": "Runaway Mana Motor",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The warning lasts until afternoon.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "A courtyard training rig screams. Its mana motor desynchronizes, the intake spiral compresses unevenly, and the containment lattice begins peeling apart.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "Input valve is jammed!",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Everyone back! If the compression chamber ruptures, the recoil will throw the rotor through the west arcade.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian can feel several patterns at once: the failing containment lattice, the overdriven rotor, and the emergency vent.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 16,
      "defaultChildId": null,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_fix_containment",
          "text": "Use Fixation on the containment lattice, then have Mira cut input.",
          "targetId": 18,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "CourtyardOutcome",
              "value": "contained"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_fix_motor",
          "text": "Use Fixation on the motor output and force the rotor to keep turning.",
          "targetId": 19,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "CourtyardOutcome",
              "value": "injured"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_evacuate",
          "text": "Do not use Fixation. Pull the emergency vent and evacuate the courtyard.",
          "targetId": 20,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "CourtyardOutcome",
              "value": "evacuated"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "name": "Containment Held",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian locks the damaged containment pattern exactly where it is.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The lattice cannot heal, but it also cannot tear any farther. Mira slams the input cutoff.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Pressure collapses. The rotor winds down inside an intact cage.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Good. You fixed the boundary, not the failure.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 17,
      "defaultChildId": 21,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "name": "The Wrong Thing to Preserve",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian fixes the motor output.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The damaged rotor obediently maintains its state while the compression stage continues feeding it energy.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Release it! You are preserving the symptom!",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The emergency vent bursts. Tavian wakes ten minutes later on the courtyard stones with ringing ears and Mira shouting his name.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "I am beginning to dislike the ground.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "The ground has a compelling case against you.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 17,
      "defaultChildId": 21,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "name": "Emergency Vent",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian ignores the tempting new power and yanks the emergency vent.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The motor destroys itself noisily but safely enough for everyone to reach cover.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Less elegant. Entirely acceptable. A ritual machine is replaceable.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 17,
      "defaultChildId": 21,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "name": "Professor Vask's Warning",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Your ability is not a shield. It is a reference.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Every stabilizing system asks some version of the same question: what state am I trying to preserve?",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "If a large enough system ever mistakes you for the answer, I would prefer not to be standing nearby.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "That was almost reassuring.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "It was not intended to be.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 18,
      "defaultChildId": 22,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "name": "The Old Calibration Manual",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Vask sends Tavian to the restricted archive to identify the pebble from memory.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The catalogue calls the material an obsolete reference aggregate: cheap mineral packed with microscopic lacery and used to teach calibration systems what 'unchanged' means.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 21,
      "defaultChildId": 24,
      "routes": [
        {
          "var": "HasPebble",
          "op": "==",
          "value": "true",
          "targetId": 23
        }
      ],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "name": "Pebble Under Glass",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Because Tavian pocketed the pebble, Vask examines it under a mana microscope.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "There. Spiral intake. Reference lattice. And a break where the release path should be.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "A handwritten appendix describes living-reference contamination.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "Read the ugly part.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "'Return the reference body to the origin geometry. Reverse intake rotation. Leave the terminal loop open. Do not permit stabilization.'",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "Obsolete safety procedure. I have never seen it used on a person.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 22,
      "defaultChildId": 25,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "name": "Diagram of a Reference Stone",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Without the pebble itself, Tavian finds a diagram that matches the grooves he saw in the classroom.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "A handwritten appendix describes living-reference contamination.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "'Return the reference body to the origin geometry. Reverse intake rotation. Leave the terminal loop open. Do not permit stabilization.'",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "That sounds uncomfortably specific.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Professor Orena Vask",
          "text": "It also sounds three centuries out of date. Do not improvise with it.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 22,
      "defaultChildId": 25,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "name": "Founders' Concordance",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "That evening, Lavernus Academy performs its annual Founders' Concordance: a calibration pulse through the academy ward network and the surrounding district.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "You can feel the towers synchronize from here.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The first pulse passes through Tavian.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "His Fixation answers.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "For one impossible instant, every ward, motor, accumulator, bridge, and stabilizer connected to the network seems to ask the same question.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "What state should remain unchanged?",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian sees a hospital window. A coat on a chair. Mira holding a week of missed notes.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Then everything turns white.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 23,
      "defaultChildId": 2,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "name": "The Grooves",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian traces the grooves in the pebble. The moment his finger reaches the spiral, the strange pressure behind his eyes returns.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The pattern wants to be followed in the direction it was cut.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "For no reason Tavian can explain, doing exactly what the pattern wants feels dangerous.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 4,
      "defaultChildId": 5,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_follow_cut",
          "text": "Follow the groove in the direction it was cut.",
          "targetId": 5,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_trace_backward",
          "text": "Trace the spiral backward.",
          "targetId": 31,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "name": "The Open Loop",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The spiral responds backward. A cold line of mana runs from the pebble into Tavian's hand.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "At the outer edge, one narrow gap remains between the beginning and the end of the pattern.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 30,
      "defaultChildId": 5,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_close_loop",
          "text": "Close the final gap with your finger.",
          "targetId": 5,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_leave_open",
          "text": "Stop before the gap and touch the center instead.",
          "targetId": 32,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "name": "Refuse Stabilization",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The pattern opens instead of completing.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian feels the same impossible certainty he felt at the hospital: a state waiting to be held.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "He could force it still. It would be easy.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Or he could stop holding anything at all.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 31,
      "defaultChildId": 5,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_stabilize_again",
          "text": "Push mana in until the pattern stabilizes.",
          "targetId": 5,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_release_power",
          "text": "Relax and let the pattern collapse.",
          "targetId": 33,
          "effects": [
            {
              "var": "PowerReleased",
              "value": "true"
            }
          ],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "name": "No Reference",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The Fixation vanishes so abruptly that Tavian nearly falls.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The pebble cracks down the spiral and becomes exactly what it always looked like: an ordinary stone.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "...Mira is going to ask why I am late.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "On the way to class, Tavian touches a flickering ward.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "It keeps flickering.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 32,
      "defaultChildId": 34,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 34,
      "name": "The Bell Passes",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The Founders' Concordance rings that evening.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian braces for a sensation he cannot name.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The pulse passes through him and continues down the street.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Nothing asks him what should remain unchanged.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "He goes to sleep.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Morning comes.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "You're staring at the date board.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "I just wanted to make sure it changed.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 33,
      "defaultChildId": 35,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 35,
      "name": "A Broken Ward, No Shortcut",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "On the new morning, a workshop ward fails beside a charging accumulator.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "Input is still climbing.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Yesterday, Tavian could have grabbed the pattern and forced it to stay intact.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Today, his hand is only a hand.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 34,
      "defaultChildId": null,
      "routes": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "o_try_fixation",
          "text": "Try Fixation anyway.",
          "targetId": 36,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_use_lesson",
          "text": "Reduce input below safe throughput, vent the buffer, then rebuild the stabilizer.",
          "targetId": 37,
          "effects": [],
          "routes": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 36,
      "name": "Nothing Happens",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Tavian reaches for the old sensation.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "Nothing happens.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "Tavian! The valve!",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "He snaps back to the problem, cuts the input, vents the buffer, and helps Mira rebuild the damaged stabilizer by hand.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "That was much harder.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "You sound disappointed to be normal.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 35,
      "defaultChildId": 38,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 37,
      "name": "Do It the Slow Way",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "Cut input to below ten Ma per second. Vent the buffer while I rebuild the stabilizer.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "You remembered the lecture.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "I remember the part about craters.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "It takes two people, three tools, and far longer than Fixation would have taken.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "The ward stabilizes anyway.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 35,
      "defaultChildId": 38,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "id": 38,
      "name": "Tomorrow",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "After class, Tavian and Mira walk beneath the academy clocks.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Mira Dain",
          "text": "Anything exciting planned for tomorrow?",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "No.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Tavian Rell",
          "text": "That sounds perfect.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "text": "For the first time in a long while, tomorrow arrives without needing permission.",
          "portrait": "",
          "background": ""
        }
      ],
      "defaultParentId": 36,
      "defaultChildId": null,
      "routes": [],
      "options": []
    }
  ]
}